Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Hoist shared isSafeUrl to @wafflebase/core, reuse in
 Sheets

The review panel flagged that the new Sheets url-detect reimplemented
the isSafeUrl / SAFE_PROTOCOLS URL-safety primitive already exported by
@wafflebase/docs, and the copy had diverged (docs allowed tel: and
resolved relative inputs against a base URL; sheets did neither).

Move the primitive to a shared @wafflebase/core/url module (both packages
already depend on core) so hyperlinks in every engine gate against one
protocol allowlist. Docs and Sheets now import it; the divergent copies
are removed. The docs behaviour change is inert in practice: all real
callers pass absolute, already-normalized URLs, so dropping the base-URL
fallback only tightens the gate against relative/invalid input.

